SUMMARY:Toronto Botanical Gardens Free Concert & Dance (Lawrence/ Leslie)
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\nNote: Members will gather at the meetup sp
 ot to enter together as a group\, as this event will no longer be hosted.\
 n\nOn **Thursday\, August 13th\, come to the Toronto Botanical Gardens for
  a Free Concert with Classical Ballet and Contemporary Dance.** There will
  also be pre-show activities that night - **Discovery Cart** to learn abou
 t plants\, **Plant/ Seed Swap**\, and an **Eco-station** to support their 
 waste diversion and recycling program. A **Restaurant** is also onsite wit
 h a selection of food and beverages\, This is an outdoor event and concert
 s proceed rain or shine. However\, if there is constant rain\, I will post
  a comment maximum 3 hours before that I will not be attending\, and atten
 dees can still choose to stay for the concert. Chairs are provided\, first
  come. If you plan to arrive late\, bring your own chair.\n\n**Concert wit
 h classical ballet and contemporary dance**\nLed by pianist Chris Au\, the
  extraordinary musicians of *Joy of Music* perform a gorgeous array of con
 cert pieces brought vividly to life by dancers from the worlds of classica
 l ballet and contemporary dance. The sumptuous White Swan pas de deux is f
 eatured alongside new and recent works by esteemed Toronto choreographers 
 Jera Wolfe and Peggy Baker. A concert as lush and bounteous as the garden 
 of Joy of Music’s founder\, Mary Gore.\n\n**Music Series Host**\n**[Anwa
 r Knight](https://anwarknight.com/)** is an award-winning Canadian broadca
 ster and environmentalist with an illustrious career spanning over two dec
 ades\, during which he held pivotal roles at some of Canada’s largest ne
 wsrooms.\n\n**The Dandelion Café**\nGrab light bites or dinner on the pat
 io overlooking the concert venue (limited space). Thursday night menu incl
 udes Flank Steak\, Grilled Salmon\, Chicken Skewers\, Jack Fruit “Crab C
 ake” and special dessert features. The cafe also offers hot and cold dri
 nks\, snacks\, and ice cream.\n\n**Discovery Cart**\nExplore plants\, wild
 life\, and ecosystems through short\, interactive activities and other wee
 kly pre-show activities from 5 to 7 p.m.\n\n**Free Plant & Seed Swap**\nBr
 ing as many plants as you wish to trade. If there isn’t anything of inte
 rest on the table when you arrive\, add your plant(s) and take a ticket to
  redeem later when you see something new you’d like to try. You can also
  borrow seeds from their Seed Library for FREE!\n\n**COST**\nConcert: Free
 \n\n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **RSVP**\n* You can also just show up at any of th
 e meeting times below\n\nA reminder will be sent the day before with my ce
 ll and reminder details where to meet and when.\n\nRSVPs close 1 day prior
 . Cancellations will result in a No Show and impact future attendance.\n\n
 **MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet members at: 6:30pm in front of the Toronto Botanic
 al Gardens at 777 Lawrence Ave. E.** to go in together\n\n**Concert Start:
  7pm**\n\nConcert Length: 1 - 1.5 hours\n\nEnjoy and please post your comm
 ents in the Event after.
